= 1 + kn -k \\
= kn - k + 1
\end{align*}
To find the minimum $k$ that makes $S_{k}$ include  $2005$, the following equation should hold.
\begin{align*}
S_{k}=kn-k+1 &= 2005\\
k(n-1) &= 2004\\
k &= \frac{2004}{n-1}
\end{align*}
And since $k$ is integers, there will be the same number of positive integer values of $k$ as factors of $2004$. We decompose like this.
