To evaluate $\log_{\sqrt{5}} 125\sqrt{5}$, we can rewrite both the base and the argument in terms of powers of 5:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{5} &= 5^{\frac{1}{2}} \\
125\sqrt{5} &= 125 \cdot 5^{\frac{1}{2}} \\
&= 5^3 \cdot 5^{\frac{1}{2}} \\
&= 5^{3+\frac{1}{2}} \\
&= 5^{\frac{7}{2}}
\end{align*}
Now we can rewrite the expression using the properties of logarithms:
\begin{align*}
\log_{\sqrt{5}} 125\sqrt{5} &= \log_{5^{\frac{1}{2}}} 5^{\frac{7}{2}} \\
&= \frac{7}{2} \cdot \frac{1}{\frac{1}{2}} \cdot \log_5 5 \\
&= \frac{7}{2} \cdot 2 \cdot 1 \\
&= \boxed{7}
\end{align*}
Therefore, $\log_{\sqrt{5}} 125\sqrt{5} = 7$.

