\[ 3n \cdot (n - 1) \cdot (n + 1) = P \]

For the middle row (row representing \( n + 2 \)):
\[ (n + 2)(2n - 9) \cdot 1 = P \]

And for the third row (bottom row):
\[ 2 \cdot n \cdot (n - 1) = P \]

From the condition that all rows must have the same product \( P \), we set up the following equation for the first row:
\[ 3n \cdot (n - 1) \cdot (n + 1) = 2 \cdot n \cdot (n - 1) \implies 3(n-1)(n+1) = 2n \]

